#WRITES
#AUTO 40
#NEEDED 0
# DE-SELECTED (110k run-list, 2026-06-30). As written this probe drives
# the SARADC with the v1 register layout, but the RK3568 is a v2 part —
# so it reads a constant 0x3FF on every channel (no real stick data) and
# spends the full poll timeout on five of six channels, making it the
# slowest probe in the sweep for zero useful output. Confirmed v2 on
# hardware: channel 0 "matched" on the first poll while channels 1-5
# timed out, yet ALL SIX returned the identical 0x3FF — the fingerprint
# of reading the wrong registers, not of real conversions.
#
# Kept compiled in (not deleted) so the v2 rewrite has a home: a v2
# controller starts a conversion through CONV_CON and reads results from
# the DATA registers up around offset +0x120 (pull the exact offsets and
# the start sequence from the kernel's rockchip_saradc.c SARADC_V2_*
# defines). Flip #NEEDED back to 1 once the body below is rewritten — at
# which point this becomes the live stick/trigger validation probe.
#
# Gamepad / analog SARADC — sweep all 6 ADC channels.
#
# The SARADC reads the device's analog inputs (sticks, analog
# triggers, the HOME-button voltage ladder). This probe ungates the
# SARADC clock, then for each channel 0..5 starts a conversion,
# polls end-of-conversion, and reads the 10-bit result. Move a stick
# between runs and watch the channel values change to map which
# channel is which axis.
#
# Requires --writes (the ungate and the per-channel start are
# writes to the CRU and the SARADC).
#
# !!! CAVEAT: the RK3568 TRM documents the *v1* SARADC register
# layout used here (CTRL/DATA/STAS). Mainline Linux, however, drives
# the rk3568 SARADC as a *v2* controller (CONV_CON/STATUS/DATA at
# different offsets). If every channel reads a constant 0 or 0x3FF,
# the silicon is v2 and this probe needs the v2 offsets — which the
# TRM does not document; pull them from the kernel's
# rockchip_saradc.c. Treat a sensible, stick-tracking value as
# confirmation the v1 layout is correct on this part.
#
# Register facts (RK3568 TRM, verified):
#   CLKGATE_CON26 @ 0xFDD20368 — clk_saradc bit 8, pclk_saradc
#     bit 7 (0=on).
#   SARADC base 0xFE720000:
#     +0x00 DATA  [9:0] = result
#     +0x04 STAS  [0]   = 1 busy / 0 stop
#     +0x08 CTRL  [2:0]=channel  [3]=power/START  [5]=int_en
#                  [6]=int_status (end-of-conversion; our POLL bit)
#   Start channel n = write (int_en|power|n) = 0x28 | n to CTRL.
#   Poll CTRL bit 6 (0x40) for done, then read DATA.

LOG ungate SARADC clocks (CLKGATE_CON26 bits 7,8 -> 0)
W 0xFDD20368 0x01800000
DELAY 20000

LOG channel 0
W 0xFE720008 0x00000028
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 100000
R 0xFE720000

LOG channel 1
W 0xFE720008 0x00000029
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 100000
R 0xFE720000

LOG channel 2
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002A
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 100000
R 0xFE720000

LOG channel 3
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002B
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 100000
R 0xFE720000

LOG channel 4
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002C
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 100000
R 0xFE720000

LOG channel 5
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002D
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 100000
R 0xFE720000

LOG SARADC sweep complete
